cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "EccoPy: a data-agnostic Python implementation of the ECCO radar echo classification algorithm"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the
  papers describing the algorithm it implements, listed under references.
  EccoPy is an independent implementation; the ECCO algorithm is the work
  of U. Romatschke and M. J. Dixon, cited there.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ian Christian
    family-names: Cornejo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-7030-9790"
    affiliation: Colorado State University
repository-code: "https://github.com/iancornejo/EccoPy"
abstract: >-
  EccoPy separates convective from stratiform radar echo using the ECCO
  (Echo Classification from COnvectivity) algorithm, in four variants
  covering 1-D series, vertical cross-sections, horizontal composites and
  full 3-D volumes. It operates purely on NumPy arrays and performs no file
  I/O, making it independent of coordinate system, file format and radar
  type. The classification path is ported from the reference MATLAB ECCO-V
  and C++ ConvStratFinder implementations developed at the NSF National
  Center for Atmospheric Research.
keywords:
  - radar
  - meteorology
  - precipitation
  - convection
  - echo classification
license: BSD-3-Clause
